"Draws coherent sampled trajectories to show possible joint behavior across a forecast or predictor range.\n\nUse when: Whole-path behavior such as turning points and persistence matters. The model can generate valid joint trajectories rather than independent marginal draws.\n\nAvoid when: Many paths become unreadable or the model supplies only unrelated pointwise quantiles.\n\nVisual grammar: Horizontal position encodes time or predictor. Each line encodes one coherent sampled path; the bundle represents the declared uncertainty ensemble.\n\nBuild: Generate a documented sample of complete trajectories with preserved draw identities. Draw thin equal-weight paths using modest opacity and an explicit path-count note. Highlight an optional summary separately and explain how paths were sampled.\n\nCheck: Check points within each path belong to the same joint draw. Verify the paths obey modeled constraints and temporal dependence. Confirm no small handpicked subset is presented as representative without disclosure.\n\nPitfalls: Crossings are intrinsic to possible trajectories and must not be untangled by moving values. Prefer a fan chart or selected separate panels when overlapping paths obscure the uncertainty message.\n\nExample: Show fifty synthetic weekly demand trajectories sampled jointly from one model, alongside a clearly labeled median forecast.\n\nAlternatives: Fan chart, Confidence band, Line chart."
